<InfoLayout title="Archive & download status" description="Verified status of music-technology resources formerly associated with this domain." canonicalPath="/download/" kicker="Archive" lede="A record of what can be verified — not a mirror of files the current publisher does not own.">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0">No first-party legacy download is offered</h2>
  <p>The expired domain did not transfer copyright, source files or a licence to redistribute the former operator’s work. A broken historic link is therefore not replaced with a guessed file or an unverified copy from a third-party archive.</p>

  <h2>Verified records</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <div><dt>The Spy Guitar</dt><dd>Former sampled-instrument project. Documentation is available at <a href="/legacy/the-spy-guitar/">the archive record</a>; original files are not redistributed.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Bang My Twister</dt><dd>Former Max for Live/controller project. A related mapping remains listed at <a href="https://maps.djtechtools.com/mappings/2929" rel="noopener">DJ TechTools</a>; Auspicious Music does not mirror it.</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2>Current, original alternatives</h2>
  <p>The new publication offers methods readers can use with recordings and projects they own:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/sound-design/sampled-instruments/building-a-sampled-instrument/">Build a small sampled instrument in Ableton Live</a></li>
    <li><a href="/ableton/midi-fighter-twister-review/">Design an Ableton controller mapping before assigning controls</a></li>
    <li><a href="/music-production/ableton-project-handoff/">Package a Live Project for another computer</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Rights or provenance information</h2>
  <p>If you created one of the former resources or hold relevant rights, send the historic title, source URL and evidence of your relationship to <a href="mailto:info@matthiasramahi.de?subject=Auspicious%20Music%20archive">info@matthiasramahi.de</a>. Do not attach binaries in the first message.</p>
